{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And he continued to sin.</b> The wicked, when trouble comes upon them, are humbled, and once it passes they grow arrogant. So too you find with Pharaoh: when trouble came upon him he was humbled and confessed, saying, ״HaShem is in the right״; once it passed, ויוסף לחטוא — and he continued to sin. And we find that the pride of the wicked is the cause of their abasement: because Pharaoh grew arrogant and said, ״Who is HaShem that I should hearken to His voice״ and so on, abasement came upon him at the Sea of Reeds. Because Nebuchadnezzar grew arrogant and said (Daniel 4:27), ״הלא דא היא בבל רבתא די אנא בניתה לבית מלכו בתקף חסני וליקר הדרי״, abasement came upon him, as it says (ibid.), ״ומן אנשא לך טרדין ועם חיות ברא מדורך עשבא כתורין לך יטעמון ושבעה עדנין יחלפון עלך״. So you see that from pride comes abasement. But the righteous do not grow arrogant; rather, they humble themselves, and from their lowliness they attain greatness and honor, as King Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Proverbs 29:23): ״גאות אדם תשפילנו ושפל רוח יתמוך כבוד״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:22.984221024Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}